 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Degenerate Elements:** Irregular shapes and partitioning can result in concavities and holes. Rays may enter and exit multiple exterior faces. Connectivity information is crucial for correct traversal [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** Adaptive sampling increases rendering time significantly. Fixed sampling is often used despite potentially oversampling large elements with constant values [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** The integration of intensity involves nested integrals. Numerical approximation (Trapezoid rule, Gaussian Quadrature) is necessary as analytic solutions are often impossible due to non-polynomial transfer functions [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Degenerate Elements:** Irregular shapes and partitioning can result in concavities and holes [S1, unofficial]. Rays may enter and exit multiple exterior faces [S1, unofficial]. Connectivity information is crucial for correct traversal [S1, unofficial].
