 ## Operating characteristics
 
-*   **Time Complexity:** Dominated by ray traversal and sampling. Adaptive sampling adds overhead; fixed sampling is simpler but may use more samples than necessary [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for element connectivity, exterior faces, and visible face lists. Parallel implementation distributes data to processors, requiring local preprocessing [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Efficient for distributed computing by minimizing communication during ray casting (local traversal). Handles irregular, unstructured grids well.
-*   **Limitations:** Preprocessing (finding visible faces) must be repeated for every view change. Adaptive sampling is expensive.
